<header class="main-header">
  <div class="series-title">Likutay Halachos &middot; Choshen Mishpat</div>
  <h1>Hilchos Da&rsquo;yonim 3 &mdash; Part 2</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Laws of Judges &mdash; 3 &middot; Osiyos 9&ndash;15</div>
</header>

<div class="continuation-note">
  Continued from Part 1 (Osiyos 1&ndash;8). Based on the teaching <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;T&rsquo;homos y&rsquo;chasyumu&rdquo;</span> in Likutay [Moharan] I, Siman 9.
</div>

<!-- ====== OS 9 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 9</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Torah</span> and <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[prayer]</span>, that both of them need one another, and one cannot exist without the other. For this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">K&rsquo;rias Sh&rsquo;ma</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the recitation of Sh&rsquo;ma]</span> and <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>, for <span class="key-term">K&rsquo;rias Sh&rsquo;ma</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Torah</span>, for the Torah is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span> <span class="key-term-def">[truth]</span>, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a Torah of truth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Malachi 2:6)</span>, for the holy Torah is the very essence of truth, for all the <span class="key-term">mitzvos</span> of the Torah are the very essence of truth. For example, the <span class="key-term">mitzvah</span> of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> <span class="key-term-def">[fringes]</span>, that Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> commanded us to place <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> on a <span class="key-term">tallis</span> &mdash; this is the very essence of truth to its truth.
</p>

<p>
However, <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> [prayer], which is the aspect of <span class="aramaic">is&rsquo;arusa dil&rsquo;sasa</span> <span class="key-term-def">[arousal from below]</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of the generality of the service that we perform and fulfill, for everything is included in the <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>; that is, that which we pray and request from Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> &mdash; in this there are many variations and shades. For certainly not everyone merits the ultimate purpose of <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> in completeness; that is, that the <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> should be included in His unity, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;He is your praise and He is your G-d&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 10:21)</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of the very essence of truth. But the common people certainly do not merit this. And each person merits <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> according to the aspect of the point of truth that he strengthens himself and exerts himself to draw himself toward the truth.
</p>

<p>
And this truth is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">chalon</span> <span class="key-term-def">[window]</span> that receives the light, as explained above &mdash; in which there are many shades without measure, according to the magnitude of the truth that one possesses, as above. It emerges, then, that <span class="key-term">Torah</span> and <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> are the aspects of the <span class="key-term">even tov</span> <span class="key-term-def">[precious stone]</span> and the <span class="key-term">chalon</span> <span class="key-term-def">[window]</span> mentioned above &mdash; which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">chamah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[sun]</span> and the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[moon]</span>, which are the aspects of <span class="key-term">Torah</span> and <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>, as is known &mdash; which are the aspects of the <span class="key-term">Torah Shebichsav</span> <span class="key-term-def">[Written Torah]</span> and the <span class="key-term">Torah Sheb&rsquo;al Peh</span> <span class="key-term-def">[Oral Torah]</span>, as is brought.
</p>

<p>
And this is what Rabbainu, <em>zichrono livrachah</em>, wrote there regarding the statement of <span class="key-term">Rabbah bar bar Chanah</span>, who was asked: <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;How far are we from the water?&rdquo;</span> &mdash; meaning, from <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> in completeness. He answered him: <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;Eight <em>parsa&rsquo;os</em> [parasangs].&rdquo;</span> And he [Rabbainu] wrote there that this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Torah</span> and <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>, which are the five <span class="key-term">Chumshay Torah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[Books of the Torah]</span> and three <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillos</span> <span class="key-term-def">[prayers]</span> per day, etc. And at first glance this is puzzling, for previously Rabbainu did not mention there at all anything about Torah being connected to <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>. But according to what was explained above, it is explained well, for the rectification of <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> is through <span class="key-term">emes</span> [truth], and <span class="key-term">emes</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Torah</span>, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a Torah of truth,&rdquo;</span> as above.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">K&rsquo;rias Sh&rsquo;ma</span> and <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">s&rsquo;michas g&rsquo;ulah lis&rsquo;fillah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[juxtaposing the [blessing of] redemption to the prayer]</span>. For <span class="key-term">K&rsquo;rias Sh&rsquo;ma</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Torah</span>, the aspect of the very essence of <span class="key-term">emes</span>, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem is our G-d, Hashem is One&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 6:4)</span>, which is the very essence of truth. And afterward we pray, which is the <span class="aramaic">is&rsquo;arusa dil&rsquo;sasa</span> [arousal from below]; that is, we arouse ourselves and prepare ourselves to pray before Him, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, and to request our needs. And this is according to the truth that each and every person possesses. And this truth is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">chalon</span> [window], as above, which needs to receive the light from the very essence of truth, which is the aspect of Torah, the aspect of <span class="key-term">K&rsquo;rias Sh&rsquo;ma</span>, as above.
</p>

<p>
For this is a great principle: that every aspect is comprised of all the aspects, and there are many aspects within each and every aspect. And therefore, even though in the aforementioned teaching it is explained that within the <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> itself there is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">precious stone</span> and a <span class="key-term">window</span>, nevertheless, the generality of the <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> of the common people is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span> relative to the <span class="key-term">tzadik</span> of the generation, who is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">precious stone</span>, as above. And likewise, the generality of <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> [moon], relative to the <span class="key-term">Torah</span>, which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">chamah</span> [sun], the aspect of a <span class="key-term">precious stone</span>, as above.
</p>

<div class="word-note">
<strong>Key structure:</strong> Torah = <em>emes</em> = <em>even tov</em> (precious stone) = <em>chamah</em> (sun) = shines of its own. T&rsquo;fillah = <em>chalon</em> (window) = <em>l&rsquo;vanah</em> (moon) = receives light from another. <em>K&rsquo;rias Sh&rsquo;ma</em> (Torah/truth) must precede and illuminate <em>t&rsquo;fillah</em> (prayer/request). The &ldquo;eight parasangs&rdquo; of Rabbah bar bar Chanah = 5 Books of Torah + 3 daily prayers.
</div>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 10 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 10</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">s&rsquo;michas g&rsquo;ulah lis&rsquo;fillah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[juxtaposing redemption to prayer]</span>, for the essential <span class="key-term">g&rsquo;ulah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[redemption]</span> is through <span class="key-term">emes</span> [truth], which is <span class="key-term">Moshiach Tzidkainu</span> <span class="key-term-def">[our righteous Messiah]</span> &mdash; who will come speedily in our days &mdash; who is called &ldquo;<span class="key-term">emes</span>,&rdquo; as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Send Your light and Your truth; they shall lead me, they shall bring me etc.&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 43:3)</span> &mdash; which Rashi explained as referring to <span class="key-term">Moshiach</span>, as is brought. For the essential coming of <span class="key-term">Moshiach</span> is to reveal the truth in the world, for then will be fulfilled: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Truth shall sprout from the earth etc.&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 85:12)</span>. And as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;The lip of truth shall be established forever&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Proverbs 12:19)</span>. <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Shall be established&rdquo;</span> [<em>tikon</em>] is written, not <span class="scripture">&ldquo;has been established&rdquo;</span> [<em>kon&rsquo;nata</em>] &mdash; for now the truth is in a great exile, and the truth has become scattered into separate flocks, and each and every person says that the truth is with him. And it is impossible to clarify the truth except for each individual according to what he estimates in his heart &mdash; he can understand a little of the truth. And the essential truth will be revealed through <span class="key-term">Moshiach</span>, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the lip of truth shall be established&rdquo;</span> etc. And this is the essential <span class="key-term">g&rsquo;ulah</span> [redemption], as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Come, gaze from the peak of <em>amanah</em> [faith]&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Song of Songs 4:8)</span>. And <span class="key-term">emunah</span> [faith] depends upon <span class="key-term">emes</span> [truth], for <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;Tzedek, when joined with emes, becomes emunah&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Zohar, Balak 120)</span>.
</p>

<p>
It emerges that the essential <span class="key-term">g&rsquo;ulah</span> is through <span class="key-term">emes</span>. And therefore the essential <span class="key-term">birchas hag&rsquo;ulah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[blessing of the redemption]</span> &mdash; that is, the blessing of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Who redeemed Yisroel&rdquo;</span> &mdash; begins with <span class="scripture">&ldquo;<em>Emes</em> v&rsquo;yatziv v&rsquo;nachon&rdquo;</span> <span class="key-term-def">[&ldquo;True and firm and correct&rdquo;]</span> etc., and speaks only of truth, for <span class="key-term">emes</span> is mentioned there <strong>eight times</strong>, because the essential <span class="key-term">g&rsquo;ulah</span> is <span class="key-term">emes</span>, as above &mdash; through which one redeems the <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> from exile and merits to pray. For it is impossible to exit from the exile of the darkness that intensifies at the time of prayer except through <span class="key-term">emes</span>, as above.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of: between <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem your G-d&rdquo;</span> and <span class="scripture">&ldquo;<em>emes</em> v&rsquo;yatziv&rdquo;</span> one should not make an interruption &mdash; for it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Hashem <em>Elokim</em> is truth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Jeremiah 10:10)</span>. For the <span class="key-term">emes</span> is comprised of the two aforementioned aspects, which are the aspects of the <span class="key-term">precious stone</span> and the <span class="key-term">window</span>. For the <span class="key-term">chamah</span> [sun] and the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> [moon] are the aspects of <span class="key-term">Torah</span> and <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> etc., as above. And these two aspects are the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Shem Molei</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the Full Name]</span>, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem <em>Elokim</em>.&rdquo;</span> For they are the aspects of the light of the sun and the moon, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;For a sun and a shield is Hashem <em>Elokim</em>&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 84:12)</span>. For the Name of <span class="key-term">Havayah</span>, as it were, is the aspect of the very essence of truth, the illuminating aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem is my light&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 27:1)</span>, as is explained there. And &ldquo;<span class="key-term">Elokim</span>&rdquo; is the aspect of diminution and contraction of the light, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> [moon], as is known.
</p>

<p>
And the essential thing is to fill the blemish of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> [moon]; that is, to join and unify the <span class="key-term">chamah</span> and the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> together; that is, to join the two Names &mdash; <span class="key-term">Hashem</span> [and] <span class="key-term">Elokim</span> &mdash; together. For this is the essential <span class="key-term">yichud</span> <span class="key-term-def">[unification]</span>, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem is One and His Name is One&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Zechariah 14:9)</span>. &ldquo;Name&rdquo; &mdash; this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Elokim</span>, <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, as is brought. That is, for the essential thing is to join the two aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span> together; that is, to elevate and clarify the <span class="key-term">emes</span> that is clothed in this world &mdash; which is the aspect of the light of the point of truth that each and every one of Yisroel possesses, which is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> &mdash; to join it and connect it and unify it with the very essence of the light of truth. For in truth, to its truth, everything is one.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Hashem <em>Elokim</em> is truth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Jeremiah 10:10)</span>, for this is the essential <span class="key-term">emes</span>: when these two Names &mdash; <span class="key-term">Hashem</span> [and] <span class="key-term">Elokim</span> &mdash; are joined and unified together; that is, the two aforementioned aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span>. For then is the essential completeness of the <span class="key-term">emes</span>, and the intention of the Creation is fulfilled. For the essential Creation was only for the sake of this: for Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> is the very essence of truth, as it were, and He has no need for the created beings, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, and the essential Creation was for our benefit &mdash; so that the truth should be revealed also in this world, so that we should know the truth of His existence, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, also in this world.
</p>

<p>
And this is the essential completeness and the ultimate purpose: when the <span class="key-term">emes</span> that is clothed in this world is clarified and ascends and is included in the very essence of the <span class="key-term">emes</span>, and everything becomes one. For in truth, it is all one, for <span class="key-term">emes</span> is one, as is explained elsewhere (in the words of Rabbainu in Siman 51). It is only that in this world the <span class="key-term">emes</span> has been clothed and covered and contracted into many garments. And the essential delight of the Holy One, Blessed is He, is when they recognize the truth also in this lowly world &mdash; for the sake of which He created all of Creation. That is, when the truth in this world is clarified until they know, also in this world, the truth to its truth. For this is the essential completeness of the light of truth, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;as the advantage of light from darkness&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Ecclesiastes 2:13)</span>. For in a place where there is no falsehood at all, it is not relevant to speak the word &ldquo;truth,&rdquo; for the essential <span class="key-term">emes</span> exists in a place where there is truth and falsehood, for then it is relevant to say that such-and-such is the truth, and not like the one who claims falsely; rather, the truth is as this one says. And therefore the essential completeness of the <span class="key-term">emes</span> is when one clarifies the truth from this world &mdash; for the sake of which everything was created, as is known.
</p>

<p>
And then, when the truth is clarified from this world through our service and our prayers, then the two aforementioned aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span> are joined together &mdash; which are the aspects of <span class="key-term">Hashem Elokim</span> &mdash; and this is the essential completeness of the <span class="key-term">emes</span>, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Hashem <em>Elokim</em> is truth,&rdquo;</span> as above. And therefore between <span class="scripture">&ldquo;<em>va&rsquo;yomer</em>&rdquo;</span> <span class="key-term-def">[&ldquo;and He said,&rdquo; the concluding word of Sh&rsquo;ma]</span> and <span class="scripture">&ldquo;<em>Emes</em> v&rsquo;yatziv&rdquo;</span> one should not make an interruption; that is, between <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem your G-d&rdquo;</span> and <span class="scripture">&ldquo;truth,&rdquo;</span> as above. For <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem your G-d&rdquo;</span> &mdash; this itself is the essential completeness of the <span class="key-term">emes</span>, as above. For <span class="key-term">K&rsquo;rias Sh&rsquo;ma</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span>, as above, and this is the essential <span class="key-term">g&rsquo;ulah</span>, as above &mdash; through which one merits <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">s&rsquo;michas g&rsquo;ulah lis&rsquo;fillah</span>, as above.
</p>

<div class="word-note">
<strong>Key concepts:</strong> <em>Moshiach</em> = the ultimate revealer of <em>emes</em> in the world. The halachah not to interrupt between &ldquo;Hashem <em>Elokaichem</em>&rdquo; and &ldquo;<em>Emes</em>&rdquo; reflects the mystical unity of the two Names (<em>Hashem</em> + <em>Elokim</em>) = the two aspects of truth (essence + this-worldly) becoming one. &ldquo;Hashem <em>Elokim</em> <em>emes</em>&rdquo; (Jeremiah 10:10) = the Full Name joined = complete truth. The purpose of all Creation is that truth be recognized <em>even in this lowly world</em>, in the aspect of &ldquo;the advantage of light from darkness.&rdquo;
</div>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 11 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 11</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the <strong>eight times</strong> that &ldquo;<em>emes</em>&rdquo; is said in <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Emes v&rsquo;yatziv&rdquo;</span> &mdash; this is the aspect of the <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;eight parsa&rsquo;os&rdquo;</span> mentioned above in the aforementioned teaching, which are <span class="key-term">Torah</span> and <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>, as above; that is, the five <span class="key-term">Chumshay Torah</span> and the three <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillos</span>, which are the aspects of the <span class="key-term">precious stone</span> and the <span class="key-term">window</span>, as above, that are included together. For this is the essential completeness of the <span class="key-term">emes</span>, which is the completeness of the <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>, as above.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the joining of <span class="key-term">emes</span> and <span class="key-term">emunah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[truth and faith]</span>. For <span class="key-term">emunah</span> is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">window</span> mentioned above, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> [moon], <span class="aramaic">ispaklaryah d&rsquo;lo nahara mi&rsquo;garmah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[a lens that does not shine of its own]</span>. For <span class="key-term">emunah</span> exists only in that which one does not comprehend and know the truth to its truth, for when one knows the truth, <span class="key-term">emunah</span> is not relevant. And the essential <span class="key-term">emunah</span> exists only in the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, in the aspect of the second type of truth mentioned above. That is, even though one does not merit knowing the truth in its very essence, nevertheless, because he desires the truth &mdash; the truth to its truth &mdash; and because he yearns and draws himself only toward the truth, through this he merits to see the truth from afar, [and to recognize] that it is fitting to believe in that which is true. For through the truth that is within him, through this he receives light from the very essence of truth, and <span class="key-term">emunah</span> is drawn to him. For he gazes upon the truth, and through this he merits <span class="key-term">emunah</span>; that is, to believe in the truth even though he does not yet merit to grasp and see the very essence of the truth. Understand this.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;Tzedek, when joined with emes, becomes emunah&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Zohar)</span>. For <span class="key-term">Tzedek</span> is <span class="aramaic">Malchusa Kadisha</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the Holy Kingdom]</span>, the aspect of the diminution of the moon, as is known. For she [Malchus] is called <span class="key-term">Tzedek</span> when they [the forces of the Sitra Achara] have a hold upon her, at the time of the diminution, as is known &mdash; for then they seek to overpower the little truth and <span class="key-term">tzedek</span> and to turn it to <span class="key-term">sheker</span> [falsehood], <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>. For this is the essential occupation of the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the Other Side]</span>: to draw sustenance from the diminished truth and to turn it to falsehood, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Any falsehood that does not have truth at its beginning does not endure in the end&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Sotah 9b)</span>.
</p>

<p>
But each person must see to join <span class="key-term">Tzedek</span> with <span class="key-term">emes</span>; that is, that he should gaze only upon the truth and draw himself only toward the truth to its truth, and he should speak the utterance in truth. And then, <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;when Tzedek is joined with emes, it becomes emunah,&rdquo;</span> and he merits complete <span class="key-term">emunah</span> &mdash; to believe in the very essence of the truth that he does not yet merit to grasp. And then, through the complete <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, he is connected and included in the very essence of the truth, in the aspect of the joining of <span class="key-term">emes</span> and <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, for it is all one, as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore we say <span class="scripture">&ldquo;<em>Emes</em> v&rsquo;yatziv&rdquo;</span> <span class="key-term-def">[&ldquo;True and firm&rdquo;]</span> in <span class="key-term">Shacharis</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the morning prayer]</span>, and <span class="scripture">&ldquo;<em>Emes</em> v&rsquo;<em>emunah</em>&rdquo;</span> <span class="key-term-def">[&ldquo;True and faithful&rdquo;]</span> in <span class="key-term">Arvis</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the evening prayer]</span>. For in the morning there is the light of day, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">chamah</span> [sun], which is the aspect of the very essence of truth, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">precious stone</span>, as above. But at night it is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the lesser luminary&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 1:16)</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> [moon], the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emunah</span> that receives from the <span class="key-term">emes</span> &mdash; the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span> and <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, the aspect of <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;Tzedek, when joined with emes, becomes emunah,&rdquo;</span> as above.
</p>

<div class="word-note">
<strong>Liturgical application:</strong> The morning blessing after <em>Sh&rsquo;ma</em> is &ldquo;<em>Emes v&rsquo;yatziv</em>&rdquo; = truth firmly established = sun/precious stone = seeing truth directly. The evening blessing is &ldquo;<em>Emes v&rsquo;emunah</em>&rdquo; = truth received through faith = moon/window = truth known through believing. The 8 mentions of &ldquo;<em>emes</em>&rdquo; in the morning blessing = 5 Books + 3 prayers = the 8 <em>parsa&rsquo;os</em> of Rabbah bar bar Chanah.
</div>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 12 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 12</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the secret of <span class="key-term">ibbur</span> <span class="key-term-def">[intercalation of the year]</span>: that we are commanded to intercalate the year in order to equalize the twelve lunar months with the solar years, in order to fill the blemish of the moon so that the light of the moon should be like the light of the sun. And therefore everything depends upon the <span class="key-term">bais din</span> <span class="key-term-def">[court]</span> specifically, for the <span class="key-term">bais din</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span>, as above, for they must judge in truth etc., as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore the <span class="key-term">bais din</span> &mdash; who are the aspect of the <span class="key-term">tzadikay hador</span> <span class="key-term-def">[righteous ones of the generation]</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span> &mdash; they know how to intercalate years and establish new months, in order to equalize the sun with the moon &mdash; which are the two aforementioned aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span> &mdash; so that the light of the moon should be like the light of the sun; that is, that the truth in this world &mdash; which is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> &mdash; should be included in the very essence of the truth, which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">chamah</span>, as above.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 13 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 13</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <strong>two witnesses</strong>, who clarify the truth. For the two witnesses are in the aspect of the two aforementioned aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span>, the aspects of the <span class="key-term">chamah</span> and the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> [sun and moon], which are the aspects of day and night, Torah and t&rsquo;fillah &mdash; which is the aspect of heaven and earth, as is known. For this is the aspect of two witnesses, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;I call to witness against you today the heavens and the earth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 4:26)</span>. And this is the aspect of the sun and the moon, the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And his throne is as the sun before Me; as the moon it shall be established forever &mdash; and a witness in the sky, faithful, forever&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 89:37&ndash;38)</span>.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the totality of the Torah, which is comprised of the two aforementioned aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Torah Shebichsav</span> [Written Torah] and <span class="key-term">Torah Sheb&rsquo;al Peh</span> [Oral Torah], as above. And the totality of the Torah is called <span class="key-term">aidus</span> <span class="key-term-def">[testimony]</span>, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And you shall place into the Ark the <em>aidus</em> [testimony] that I shall give to you&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 25:16)</span>. For the <span class="key-term">aidus</span> [testimony/witnesses] clarify the truth. And the essential clarification of the truth is when the two aforementioned aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span> are joined together.
</p>

<p>
For the <span class="key-term">sheker</span> [falsehood] has no hold except through the second type of truth mentioned above, which is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, as above. For in truth, Yisroel are not suspected of falsehood, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;The remnant of Yisroel shall not do iniquity, nor speak lies etc.&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Zephaniah 3:13)</span>. And therefore in truth we do not suspect the litigant who denies [owing] his fellow&rsquo;s money of wanting to rob him through complete falsehood, for <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;there is a presumption that a person does not act brazenly before his creditor&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Bava Kama 107a)</span>. Rather, we say: <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;He is only evading [for time], reasoning: when I have the money I will pay him&rdquo;</span> &mdash; or he has a possible claim of an old loan against him, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said regarding the laws of one who <span class="key-term">admits to part</span> [of a claim] and <span class="key-term">denies the whole</span> <span class="source">(Bava Metzia 3a and following)</span>.
</p>

<p>
It emerges that we do not suspect him of complete falsehood; rather, he permits himself and covers the falsehood with truth. And all of this results from the aspect of the diminished truth &mdash; which is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span> &mdash; for because of the contraction of the truth, the truth has become so covered for him that he wishes to cover the falsehood with truth and permits himself [the transgression] and denies his fellow&rsquo;s money.
</p>

<p>
And therefore it is impossible to clarify the truth to its truth except when one illuminates from the very essence of truth &mdash; which is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">precious stone</span> &mdash; into the aspect of truth that is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, and one joins and unifies both of them together &mdash; which is the aspect of the joining of the <span class="key-term">chamah</span> and the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span>. And then the aspect of the truth that is clothed in this world &mdash; which is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span> &mdash; is strengthened and clarified. And when this truth is clarified and included in its root &mdash; in the very essence of the truth &mdash; then <span class="scripture">&ldquo;all the workers of iniquity shall be scattered&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 92:10)</span>, for the falsehood falls and is completely nullified. For the essential hold of the falsehood was only from the weakening of the truth &mdash; that this truth, the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, was weakened and contracted so much that a hold descended from it to the falsehood. But when this truth is clarified and joined with the very essence of the truth, then the falsehood is completely nullified, as above.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <strong>two witnesses</strong>. For two witnesses who testify together about one matter &mdash; this is the aspect of the joining of the <span class="key-term">chamah</span> and the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span>, which are the aspects of the <span class="scripture">&ldquo;great luminary&rdquo;</span> and the <span class="scripture">&ldquo;lesser luminary&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 1:16)</span>, which are the two aforementioned aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span>. For this is a principle: that no two <span class="key-term">n&rsquo;shomos</span> <span class="key-term-def">[souls]</span> are equal in the world; rather, one is greater than his fellow. And therefore these two witnesses who testify together &mdash; certainly one is greater than his fellow, as it is written in the <span class="key-term">Mishnah</span>: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;How does one examine the witnesses? They bring in the greater one first etc.&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Sanhedrin 3:6)</span> &mdash; for certainly one is great and one is small.
</p>

<p>
And &ldquo;great&rdquo; and &ldquo;small&rdquo; &mdash; this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">chamah</span> and the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span>, the aspect of the <span class="scripture">&ldquo;great luminary&rdquo;</span> and the <span class="scripture">&ldquo;lesser luminary.&rdquo;</span> For this is the essential distinction and level that exists among the <span class="key-term">n&rsquo;shomos</span>, for the <span class="key-term">n&rsquo;shamah</span> [soul] is called &ldquo;light,&rdquo; as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;The lamp of Hashem is the soul of man&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Proverbs 20:27)</span>. And the essential light of the <span class="key-term">n&rsquo;shamah</span> is <span class="key-term">emes</span>, which is the essential light that illuminates. And every <span class="key-term">n&rsquo;shamah</span> that possesses more truth is greater and illuminates more. And the light of the greater one, relative to his fellow who is smaller than him, is in the aspect of a <span class="key-term">precious stone</span> relative to a <span class="key-term">window</span>, for the smaller one needs to receive from the greater one, for all the <span class="key-term">n&rsquo;shomos</span> receive one from another, from level to level.
</p>

<p>
It emerges that when two people testify together about one matter, this is the aspect of the joining of the two aforementioned aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span>, which are the aspects of the <span class="key-term">chamah</span> and the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span>, as above. And through this is the essential clarification of the truth, as above. For the essential clarification of the truth is when the truth in this world &mdash; the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span> &mdash; is joined and included in the very essence of the truth. For this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Shem Molei</span> [Full Name], the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Hashem <em>Elokim</em> is truth.&rdquo;</span> And therefore two witnesses have trustworthiness forever, and <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;two are like a hundred&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Makkos 5b)</span> &mdash; for the essential clarification of the truth is through the joining of the two aforementioned aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span>, as above.
</p>

<div class="word-note">
<strong>Key parallel:</strong> Two witnesses = sun and moon = Written Torah and Oral Torah = <em>even tov</em> and <em>chalon</em> = two types of truth joining together. The Mishnah&rsquo;s instruction to &ldquo;bring in the greater one first&rdquo; reflects the inherent hierarchy of souls &mdash; one witness is always &ldquo;greater&rdquo; (sun/precious stone), the other &ldquo;lesser&rdquo; (moon/window). Their joint testimony = joining of the two Names (<em>Hashem Elokim</em>) = clarification of truth. Falsehood feeds parasitically on a diminished truth (window dimmed); the joining of the two aspects of truth expels falsehood entirely.
</div>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 14 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 14</div>

<p>
And therefore the witnesses must have their testimony <span class="key-term">m&rsquo;chuvenes</span> <span class="key-term-def">[aligned/matching]</span>. For <span class="key-term">emes</span> is one, and the two of them must be joined together so that the two aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span> are included together, for it is all one.
</p>

<p>
However, nevertheless, the essential thing is that they should align together in the essential matter of the testimony. But if they contradicted one another in the <span class="key-term">b&rsquo;dikos</span> <span class="key-term-def">[ancillary examinations]</span>, their testimony remains valid, as is brought in the words of our Sages, of blessed memory, in the <span class="key-term">Gemara</span> <span class="source">(Sanhedrin 40a and following)</span>. That is, as above: for the truth in this world is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, and it is impossible for the truth to be entirely clear for each and every person. And nevertheless, it is truth so long as one guards the truth so that it should not be turned to falsehood, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>; rather, one gazes upon the truth to its truth. For then, even though one does not yet merit the truth that is clear to the very essence of truth, nevertheless, another can illuminate within it, and one can exit through this from darkness to light.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the above: that even though one of the witnesses erred slightly in the <span class="key-term">b&rsquo;dikos</span> [ancillary examinations] and did not merit to discern the truth in its very essence, in its ultimate exactitude &mdash; nevertheless, since in the essential matter of the testimony he aligns with his fellow, therefore we believe him that his words are true, and we accept his testimony. For the two aspects of truth are included together and illuminate one within the other, and they repel the falsehood of the litigants. For when the two aspects of truth are joined together, the falsehood is repelled &mdash; and this is the aspect of two witnesses.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 15 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 15</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">sh&rsquo;vuah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[oath]</span> that they impose upon the litigant in order to clarify the truth when there are no witnesses to testify. For the one who denies [owing] his fellow &mdash; certainly he is not suspected of complete falsehood, as above; rather, he covers the falsehood with truth, and <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;he is only evading [for time]&rdquo;</span> etc., as above. And all of this is because the truth has been weakened and diminished &mdash; which is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span> &mdash; because it does not receive from the very essence of truth. For this is the essential aspect of the blemish of the moon: when she is not unified and joined with the sun, which is the aspect of the very essence of truth, as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;the Merciful One imposed an oath upon him, so that he should admit&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Shavuos 40b)</span>. For the <span class="key-term">sh&rsquo;vuah</span> [oath] is the aspect of the Name of Hashem, which is the aspect of the very essence of truth. For a <span class="key-term">sh&rsquo;vuah</span> is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">Tzadik</span>, as is brought. And therefore the <span class="key-term">sh&rsquo;vuah</span> is [administered while] holding a sacred object &mdash; that is, a <span class="key-term">Seifer Torah</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of the very essence of truth, as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore, through the <span class="key-term">sh&rsquo;vuah</span> &mdash; which is the Name of Hashem, which is the aspect of the very essence of truth &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Give truth to Yaakov etc., that You swore to our forefathers etc.&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Michah 7:20)</span> &mdash; therefore, through the <span class="key-term">sh&rsquo;vuah</span>, the truth is revealed and clarified, and the falsehood is repelled, by means of the very essence of truth &mdash; which is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">sh&rsquo;vuah</span> &mdash; illuminating into the aspect of truth that is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>. And then the truth in this world is strengthened and included in the very essence of truth, and then the falsehood is repelled, as above.
</p>

<div class="word-note">
<strong>Halachic-mystical parallel:</strong> The oath (<em>sh&rsquo;vuah</em>) imposed by the court = the Name of Hashem = the very essence of truth = the sun/precious stone, shining its essential light into the diminished truth (the window/moon) of the litigant. The <em>sh&rsquo;vuah</em> is administered while holding a <em>Seifer Torah</em> because Torah = very essence of truth. The verse &ldquo;Give truth to Yaakov &hellip; that You <em>swore</em> to our forefathers&rdquo; (Michah 7:20) connects &ldquo;truth&rdquo; and &ldquo;oath&rdquo; (<em>nishbata</em>) &mdash; the oath evokes the essential truth and causes the litigant to admit.
</div>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== TRANSLATOR SUMMARY ====== -->
<div class="translator-summary">
<h3>Translator&rsquo;s Summary &mdash; Osiyos 9&ndash;15</h3>

<p>
These seven sections develop the grand correspondence between the structure of daily prayer and the structure of the court system. The two foundational metaphors from the teaching in Siman 9 &mdash; the <em>even tov</em> (precious stone, self-luminous) and the <em>chalon</em> (window, receiving light from another) &mdash; are now mapped onto a web of halachic institutions:
</p>

<div class="flowchart">
<h4>The Web of Correspondences (Osiyos 9&ndash;15)</h4>
<div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-arrow">&diams;</span><span class="flow-text"><strong>Precious Stone / Sun / Havayah</strong> = Torah = <em>K&rsquo;rias Sh&rsquo;ma</em> = essential truth = Written Torah = the &ldquo;greater&rdquo; witness = the oath (<em>sh&rsquo;vuah</em>) = the <em>tzadik</em> of the generation</span></div>
<div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-arrow">&diams;</span><span class="flow-text"><strong>Window / Moon / Elokim</strong> = T&rsquo;fillah = prayer = <em>emunah</em> = Oral Torah = the &ldquo;lesser&rdquo; witness = the ordinary Jew&rsquo;s truth = <em>Malchus</em></span></div>
<div class="flow-connector">&darr;</div>
<div class="flow-step"><span class="flow-arrow">&diams;</span><span class="flow-text"><strong>Their Union</strong> = <em>s&rsquo;michas g&rsquo;ulah lis&rsquo;fillah</em> (juxtaposing redemption to prayer) = &ldquo;Hashem <em>Elokim</em> <em>emes</em>&rdquo; = 8 mentions of <em>emes</em> in <em>Emes v&rsquo;yatziv</em> = 5 Chumashim + 3 t&rsquo;fillos = the two witnesses testifying together = <em>ibbur</em> (intercalation equalizing sun and moon) = the complete clarification of truth = the nullification of falsehood</span></div>
</div>

<p>
<strong>Os 9</strong> establishes the Torah/t&rsquo;fillah duality as sun/moon, precious stone/window, with a key insight: each person&rsquo;s prayer reflects his degree of truth, while Torah is inherently essential truth. <strong>Os 10</strong> introduces <em>g&rsquo;ulah</em> (redemption) as the product of <em>emes</em> &mdash; <em>Moshiach</em> will reveal truth fully &mdash; and explains the no-interruption rule between <em>Sh&rsquo;ma</em> and <em>Emes v&rsquo;yatziv</em> as the unification of <em>Hashem</em> and <em>Elokim</em>. A profound point: the purpose of Creation itself is that truth be recognized in this lowly world where falsehood exists, since without the contrast of falsehood, the word &ldquo;truth&rdquo; has no meaning. <strong>Os 11</strong> differentiates the morning and evening blessings (<em>Emes v&rsquo;yatziv</em> vs. <em>Emes v&rsquo;emunah</em>) as day/night, sun/moon, direct knowledge vs. faithful belief. <strong>Os 12</strong> returns to the <em>bais din</em>: intercalation of the calendar (equalizing sun and moon) depends on the court because the court embodies truth. <strong>Os 13</strong> explains two witnesses as two aspects of truth joining (sun+moon, great luminary + lesser luminary, greater soul + lesser soul); their combined testimony expels falsehood. A key halachic principle is given mystical grounding: we do not suspect a denier of outright lying &mdash; rather, his diminished truth (weakened window) has allowed falsehood to cover itself in truth. <strong>Os 14</strong> explains why witnesses need only agree on essentials, not peripherals &mdash; no one in this world has perfectly clear truth, yet even imperfect truth is a valid window through which the essential truth can illuminate. <strong>Os 15</strong> explains the <em>sh&rsquo;vuah</em> (oath) as the essential truth (Name of Hashem, Torah scroll) illuminating into the diminished truth of the litigant &mdash; like the sun filling the moon&rsquo;s blemish.
</p>

<p class="translator-note">
&mdash; Translator&rsquo;s summary. Not part of the original text.
</p>
</div>

